WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.013
- Hey ya'll we're back with
my friend Garth Brooks!

00:00:03.013 --> 00:00:04.197
- [Kelly] Wooo!

00:00:04.197 --> 00:00:05.188
(crowd cheering)

00:00:05.188 --> 00:00:06.600
(Garth laughing)

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:07.683
- That would've been my sound at your show

00:00:07.683 --> 00:00:08.918
when I was a kid.

00:00:08.918 --> 00:00:09.751
Ahhhhh.

00:00:10.640 --> 00:00:11.473
- He's got --

00:00:11.473 --> 00:00:12.306
I'm crazy.

00:00:12.306 --> 00:00:13.717
I just saw myself.

00:00:13.717 --> 00:00:14.550
(Kelly laughing)

00:00:14.550 --> 00:00:18.740
- He's got a new vinyl
box set called Legacy,

00:00:18.740 --> 00:00:20.220
and we're breaking down his career,

00:00:20.220 --> 00:00:21.160
so far,

00:00:21.160 --> 00:00:23.050
with a look at his
albums in the collection.

00:00:23.050 --> 00:00:25.910
Next, let's talk about
Garth's second live album,

00:00:25.910 --> 00:00:27.070
Triple Live.

00:00:27.070 --> 00:00:29.860
These are all songs you
recorded during your world tour?

00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:31.040
- [Garth] Yeah, during the comeback tour.

00:00:31.040 --> 00:00:33.343
- I saw the show and it was incredible.

00:00:35.400 --> 00:00:37.050
- So Garth's wife Trisha Yearwood,

00:00:37.050 --> 00:00:39.820
my favorite singer on the planet,

00:00:39.820 --> 00:00:42.200
was featured in two songs
on Triple Live, right?

00:00:42.200 --> 00:00:43.270
- Yeah, she's the bomb.

00:00:43.270 --> 00:00:44.550
- She's so good!

00:00:44.550 --> 00:00:45.383
- So you know, when people go,

00:00:45.383 --> 00:00:46.500
"Have you been singing together forever?",

00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.333
Well, yeah.

00:00:47.333 --> 00:00:48.730
I mean she has sang on,

00:00:48.730 --> 00:00:49.970
we counted it up the other day,

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:50.803
just out of fun.

00:00:50.803 --> 00:00:53.600
I think she's sang on over
90 songs in our career,

00:00:53.600 --> 00:00:55.130
that's her singing the background vocals

00:00:55.130 --> 00:00:55.963
from way back,

00:00:55.963 --> 00:00:56.796
first record

00:00:56.796 --> 00:00:57.629
to here.

00:00:57.629 --> 00:00:58.908
So she's as much the Garth Brooks sound,

00:00:58.908 --> 00:01:00.563
or the cooler part of it,

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:02.303
than Garth is,

00:01:02.303 --> 00:01:03.740
so she's great.

00:01:03.740 --> 00:01:05.073
And all the same players
have played on every record.

00:01:05.073 --> 00:01:06.900
- So you record with Trisha all the time,

00:01:06.900 --> 00:01:07.852
and I work with my husband.

00:01:07.852 --> 00:01:08.685
You know, Brandon.

00:01:08.685 --> 00:01:09.880
And, is it hard,

00:01:09.880 --> 00:01:12.320
like, to do it on the
road, and work together,

00:01:12.320 --> 00:01:13.170
because you're both artists,

00:01:13.170 --> 00:01:14.220
like, Brandon and I, my husband and I,

00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.590
he's my manager and I'm an artist.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:16.640
We're very different.

00:01:16.640 --> 00:01:18.160
Is that hard, because you're both artists?

00:01:18.160 --> 00:01:19.710
- Yeah, it's also your best friend,

00:01:19.710 --> 00:01:21.199
so you got a lot of good conversations,

00:01:21.199 --> 00:01:23.170
and we all want to be like-minded,

00:01:23.170 --> 00:01:24.750
we all want to do the right thing,

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:25.890
but how we get there,

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:27.513
you're going to need all the
diversity you can, right?

00:01:27.513 --> 00:01:29.500
All the different way of
thinking that you can.

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:31.590
So me and her are always cool

00:01:31.590 --> 00:01:33.130
until

00:01:33.130 --> 00:01:34.860
it comes to music.

00:01:34.860 --> 00:01:35.750
- It just does,

00:01:35.750 --> 00:01:37.457
because you know, you look and I go,

00:01:37.457 --> 00:01:39.289
"Why do you like that
song? That song sucks."

00:01:39.289 --> 00:01:40.122
Wooop!

00:01:40.122 --> 00:01:41.280
(Kelly laughing)

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:42.357
- [Garth] And all of a sudden it's like,

00:01:42.357 --> 00:01:43.480
"Oh I didn't mean that,

00:01:43.480 --> 00:01:44.730
I really didn't mean that."

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:45.980
And it's just how it is,

00:01:45.980 --> 00:01:47.050
it's the same way with her.

00:01:47.050 --> 00:01:48.500
She'll go, "Why do you use that player."

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:49.981
And you're like, well, you know.

00:01:49.981 --> 00:01:50.814
It's just that love --

00:01:50.814 --> 00:01:52.320
- [Kelly] You're protective of your --

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:53.330
- Oh that passion.

00:01:53.330 --> 00:01:54.163
- [Kelly] Yeah

00:01:54.163 --> 00:01:54.996
- For music, it's great.

00:01:54.996 --> 00:01:56.280
So we've had some pretty good --

00:01:56.280 --> 00:01:57.113
- [Kelly] That's cool though,

00:01:57.113 --> 00:01:58.370
because then you'll call each other out.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:01:59.230
Brandon and I do that.

00:01:59.230 --> 00:02:00.063
We'll call each other out and be like,

00:02:00.063 --> 00:02:01.740
"Nah, it wasn't that great.
You could do better."

00:02:01.740 --> 00:02:02.880
- [Garth] Yeah I mean,

00:02:02.880 --> 00:02:04.240
that's what you do is, you push yourself.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:05.420
I've never said that.

00:02:05.420 --> 00:02:06.600
If he's ever said that to you,

00:02:06.600 --> 00:02:07.460
he's a braver man than me.

00:02:07.460 --> 00:02:08.500
(crowd laughing)

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:09.370
- He's pretty bold,

00:02:09.370 --> 00:02:10.926
that's why I think he's sexy.

00:02:10.926 --> 00:02:12.480
(crowd and Garth laughing)

00:02:12.480 --> 00:02:13.876
- Something weird about me, I like it.

00:02:13.876 --> 00:02:14.950
- [Kelly] So wait,

00:02:14.950 --> 00:02:15.890
this can't be right,

00:02:15.890 --> 00:02:17.410
I heard about this and I was like,

00:02:17.410 --> 00:02:19.210
surely you've done a stadium tour before,

00:02:19.210 --> 00:02:20.043
because you're Garth Brooks,

00:02:20.043 --> 00:02:21.355
but this is your first stadium tour.

00:02:21.355 --> 00:02:22.300
- [Garth] It's my first stadium tour,

00:02:22.300 --> 00:02:24.740
Try to remember that we spent
eight years in the 90's.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:25.573
- Yeah.

00:02:25.573 --> 00:02:26.710
- And then the tour was done,

00:02:26.710 --> 00:02:28.550
and so went home to raise our babies,

00:02:28.550 --> 00:02:29.750
so we started in '14,

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:32.360
so we've actually been
touring for 13 years.

00:02:32.360 --> 00:02:34.700
- [Garth] Which is crazy when
you think of it that way,

00:02:34.700 --> 00:02:36.444
and so when we came back,
we kind of put a tour

00:02:36.444 --> 00:02:38.990
just like the one we just
came off of in the late 90's,

00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.500
just kind of see where we're at.

00:02:40.500 --> 00:02:41.840
So we've never been in stadiums,

00:02:41.840 --> 00:02:42.673
but I can tell you this,

00:02:42.673 --> 00:02:45.360
I was scared to death stadiums
were going to be cold,

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.180
distant, you know?

00:02:47.180 --> 00:02:50.660
They are the warmest, coolest,

00:02:50.660 --> 00:02:51.730
because, I'm a guy,

00:02:51.730 --> 00:02:54.520
I'm the last one that
wants to say size matters.

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:55.353
It does!

00:02:55.353 --> 00:02:56.200
It does!

00:02:56.200 --> 00:02:57.900
- It's fabulous,

00:02:57.900 --> 00:02:59.020
and you know, when people sing at you,

00:02:59.020 --> 00:02:59.900
Unanswered Prayers.

00:02:59.900 --> 00:03:01.400
If you guys have been to a stadium show,

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:03.405
you could vouch for me.

00:03:03.405 --> 00:03:05.530
- 17,000 people singing Unanswered Prayers

00:03:05.530 --> 00:03:07.300
will tear your heart out.

00:03:07.300 --> 00:03:08.990
87,000!

00:03:08.990 --> 00:03:11.150
Will tear your heart out
and take you to dinner.

00:03:11.150 --> 00:03:12.670
It's fantastic!

00:03:12.670 --> 00:03:14.100
So its wonderful!

00:03:14.100 --> 00:03:16.490
- Do you get more nervous
in that environment, or no?

00:03:16.490 --> 00:03:17.323
- I don't know.

00:03:17.323 --> 00:03:18.930
It's...

00:03:18.930 --> 00:03:20.453
- Just because it's so big?

00:03:20.453 --> 00:03:22.140
I don't really see you
as nervous, actually,

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:23.090
I don't know? Do you get nervous?

00:03:23.090 --> 00:03:24.560
- You get nervous, but the truth is,

00:03:24.560 --> 00:03:26.890
you stick a guitar in between me and you,

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:27.723
then all of a sudden, I'm home.

00:03:27.723 --> 00:03:28.556
- Oh.

00:03:28.556 --> 00:03:29.970
- [Garth] So it's very sweet,

00:03:29.970 --> 00:03:30.803
these people.

00:03:30.803 --> 00:03:33.190
If it's a dive bar of 500,

00:03:33.190 --> 00:03:36.210
or if it's a stadium of
however many thousands,

00:03:36.210 --> 00:03:38.690
they allow you to suck,

00:03:38.690 --> 00:03:40.070
and be okay.

00:03:40.070 --> 00:03:41.750
They kind of let you be you, you know?

00:03:41.750 --> 00:03:43.470
- [Garth] Scars, flaws and all.

00:03:43.470 --> 00:03:44.430
It's like a woman.

00:03:44.430 --> 00:03:46.870
The most gorgeous thing a woman can wear

00:03:46.870 --> 00:03:48.904
is happiness, right?

00:03:48.904 --> 00:03:49.737
- Yeah.

00:03:49.737 --> 00:03:51.470
- When they're confident
and happy its like, whoa.

00:03:51.470 --> 00:03:53.800
And that's how they make
you feel when you walk out.

00:03:53.800 --> 00:03:56.143
That you're happy and you're confident.

00:03:56.143 --> 00:03:56.976
It's cool.

00:03:56.976 --> 00:03:58.355
- Like, what?

00:03:58.355 --> 00:03:59.880
So what I love about you too though,

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:01.590
is you're not, the stadium thing is cool,

00:04:01.590 --> 00:04:03.500
but you're also doing a dive bar tour.

00:04:03.500 --> 00:04:04.333
- Dive bars are fun.

00:04:04.333 --> 00:04:06.346
- Exactly, I love like clubs

00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:07.730
oh that's so fun.

00:04:07.730 --> 00:04:08.846
- [Garth] Because they're
loud, they're hot --

00:04:08.846 --> 00:04:09.679
- [Kelly] And intimate,

00:04:09.679 --> 00:04:10.512
and you're right in their face,

00:04:10.512 --> 00:04:11.345
and you're all sweating together --

00:04:11.345 --> 00:04:12.434
- [Garth] Everybody stinks!

00:04:12.434 --> 00:04:13.492
It's awesome.

00:04:13.492 --> 00:04:14.325
(crowd laughs)

00:04:14.325 --> 00:04:15.158
- [Garth] It's fabulous
because you're sitting there,

00:04:15.158 --> 00:04:16.860
and you're sharing the same sweat,

00:04:16.860 --> 00:04:17.955
people are, you know,

00:04:17.955 --> 00:04:19.290
you can't get to the bar,

00:04:19.290 --> 00:04:20.430
because everything is just packed,

00:04:20.430 --> 00:04:22.640
so everybody's drinking
from each others' beers.

00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:23.795
It's a family thing.

00:04:23.795 --> 00:04:24.628
- Not that.

00:04:24.628 --> 00:04:25.461
- Oh yeah, yeah.

00:04:25.461 --> 00:04:26.294
- No.

00:04:26.294 --> 00:04:27.127
- It's funny, it's old school.

00:04:27.127 --> 00:04:27.960
So it's great,

00:04:27.960 --> 00:04:30.040
and these dive bars are just cool.

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:31.490
We're about to do our last one,

00:04:31.490 --> 00:04:32.760
but I don't think so.

00:04:32.760 --> 00:04:35.130
I think I'm having such
a great freaking time,

00:04:35.130 --> 00:04:35.963
I'm going to ask if we --

00:04:35.963 --> 00:04:37.060
- I would love to see you in a dive bar!

00:04:37.060 --> 00:04:38.560
- Oh let's do it, let's do it.

